# Build-context exclusions.
#
# The context is the repository root (both Dockerfiles need to reach across
# backend/ and web/), so without this file every build would upload the host's
# .venv and node_modules -- hundreds of megabytes of Windows-linked binaries
# that would then be copied over the Linux ones installed in the image.

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Host virtualenvs and caches. A Windows .venv inside a Linux image is not
# merely useless: on a bind mount it shadows the interpreter's own packages.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Node: installed inside the image for the right platform.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state that must never be baked into an image.
**/*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/staticfiles/
**/media/
celerybeat-schedule*
**/*.log

# Docs and plans: not needed to build or run anything.
docs/
*.md
